LICENSE NOT YET CHOSEN

This is a placeholder carried in from the base template. It grants no rights to
anyone. Replace it with a real license before this code is shared outside the
organisation.

The realistic choices:

  MIT           Permissive and short, no patent grant.
  Apache-2.0    Permissive with an explicit patent grant and NOTICE handling.
  Proprietary   For a repo that stays private. Replace this file with
                "Copyright (c) <year> <owner>. All rights reserved." and
                nothing else.

https://choosealicense.com compares them.

Until this file is replaced, GitHub reports the repository as having no
recognised license. That is the intended signal, not an oversight. Default
copyright applies in the meantime: all rights reserved, whatever this file says.
